  "title": "Zhang Qian",
  "summary": "Zhang Qian was an envoy of Emperor Wu of Han, sent from the capital Chang'an in 138 BCE to seek an alliance with the Yuezhi against the Xiongnu. The Xiongnu held him for about ten years, and he returned to China in 125 or 126 BCE with reports of lands farther west. UNESCO links his mission to the Silk Roads corridor.",
